# Walkthrough: Authentication Implementation

I have implemented a complete authentication system for the Meatly application, allowing users to register, log in, and log out.

## Changes Made

### Backend
- **User Model**: Created [models.py](file:///c:/Users/AN-Raj-Dell-3420/Documents/meatly-flask/meatly-flask/models.py) with a [User](file:///c:/Users/AN-Raj-Dell-3420/Documents/meatly-flask/meatly-flask/models.py#7-19) model using `Flask-SQLAlchemy` and `Flask-Login`.
- **Authentication Routes**: Added `/login`, `/register`, and `/logout` routes to [app.py](file:///c:/Users/AN-Raj-Dell-3420/Documents/meatly-flask/meatly-flask/app.py).
- **Persistent Cart**: Integrated database storage for user carts. Items are now saved to the [User](file:///c:/Users/AN-Raj-Dell-3420/Documents/meatly-flask/meatly-flask/models.py#7-19) profile and automatically restored when the user logs in, even across different sessions.
- **Session Management**: Integrated `Flask-Login` for secure session handling and password hashing (using `Werkzeug`). Added logic to clear the [cart](file:///c:/Users/AN-Raj-Dell-3420/Documents/meatly-flask/meatly-flask/app.py#30-32) and [coupon](file:///c:/Users/AN-Raj-Dell-3420/Documents/meatly-flask/meatly-flask/app.py#214-224) from the session upon logout to prevent persistence between different guest/user states.
- **Database**: Configured SQLite database ([meatly.db](file:///c:/Users/AN-Raj-Dell-3420/Documents/meatly-flask/meatly-flask/instance/meatly.db)) to store user information.

### Frontend
- **Login Page**: Created [templates/login.html](file:///c:/Users/AN-Raj-Dell-3420/Documents/meatly-flask/meatly-flask/templates/login.html) with a modern, brand-consistent design.
- **Registration Page**: Created [templates/register.html](file:///c:/Users/AN-Raj-Dell-3420/Documents/meatly-flask/meatly-flask/templates/register.html) for new user signups.
- **Navigation Bar**: Updated [templates/base.html](file:///c:/Users/AN-Raj-Dell-3420/Documents/meatly-flask/meatly-flask/templates/base.html) to dynamically show user status and authentication links.

## Verification Results

### Manual Testing Flow
1.  **Registration**: Successfully registered a new user ("Test User").
2.  **Login**: Logged in with the new credentials. The navbar updated to show the user's name, and the cart persisted from the pre-login state.
3.  **Logout**: Logged out successfully. The navbar reverted to showing "Login" and "Join", and the cart was cleared.

